WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.050
- The thing what I love about being a chef

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.850
is to see the satisfactory
of the guests, the smile.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.470
Dubai is such a vibrant
city, diversity of people,

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.019
nationalities that we have,
it's brilliant, it's fantastic.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.500
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.280
- [Ching] Wherever I am in the world,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.870
food is the focal point
of everything I do.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.610
My name is Ching, and I'm
a TV chef and food writer.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:25.240
My taste journeys have
taken me all over the world

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.310
in search of great
flavors and new recipes.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.370
Finally, it's brought me
to Dubai, and I can't wait

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.830
to explore its rich and varied food scene,

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.253
one bite at a time.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.640
Reif Othman, internationally
celebrated chef, has worked

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.140
in a variety of kitchens, from
fine dining and experiential

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.280
cuisine to innovative pop-ups.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.210
Food and family have
always gone hand in hand

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.410
and for chef Reif, Dubai has provided

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.790
the perfect environment to raise a family

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.713
and pursue his culinary adventures.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.380
- Hi, my name is Reif Othman,
and I'm from Singapore.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.470
My family would describe
me as hard working, funny

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.400
and little bit crazy.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.785
I would describe myself easy,
free-style, very straight,

00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:09.760
on the point.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.270
So, I have two kids, Ayden and
Ally. They are my precious,

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.120
they are my life.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.250
- [Ching] My grandmother was
a very important person in my

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.430
family's life, and one of
my favorite memories of my

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.860
gran was that she'd always
make me and my brothers

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.490
packed lunches for school.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.430
I'm really excited to be meeting
a father and chef who does

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.350
the same for his children.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.990
- [Reif] So today we are
making a salmon maki roll,

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:32.870
sashimi as well.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:33.920
- [Ching] Oh wow, they're so lucky.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.860
- Yeah, yeah they're done.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.001
- Great, I'd be happy with that.

00:01:37.001 --> 00:01:40.470
- Yeah happy day.
- I mean chef's lunch box!

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.710
- It's so multi-faceted, Dubai, isn't it?

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.380
Do you feel like that's also
a mirror for who you are,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.190
you're a serious dad,
you're a serious chef.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.770
- [Reif] It's not easy,
but I have to juggle it.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.900
At home you have to be fatherly
figure, but Dubai's been

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.538
great, it's giving me
a lot of opportunity.

00:01:56.538 --> 00:01:58.530
- [Ching] After meeting
Reif's family, we head to the

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.850
waterfront fish market, so that
he could show me the amazing

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.130
variety of fresh produce
Dubai's coastline has to offer.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.180
For a chef whose passion is
seafood, I can see why Reif was

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.400
excited to bring me here.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.540
- [Reif] Welcome to
waterfront fish market.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.570
They're open 24/7 throughout the year.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.160
Let me show you some salmon fishes.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.357
- They look so fresh!
- Hi, morning.

00:02:17.357 --> 00:02:20.470
- [Reif] This is Tuna, Blue
Crab, local fishes, import,

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.554
shell fish, you just name it, we have it.

00:02:22.554 --> 00:02:23.387
- [Ching] Fantastic.

00:02:23.387 --> 00:02:25.370
All your fresh fish, this is
where you get it all from?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.220
- [Reif] Exactly, plenty of choice, yeah,

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.320
plenty of choice, yes.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.770
Once I pick some fish that I want.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:31.603
- [Ching] OK.

00:02:31.603 --> 00:02:33.200
- Maybe I bring it to my
local fish restaurant.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.033
Are you hungry?

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:34.866
- I'm always hungry.

00:02:34.866 --> 00:02:35.851
- Let's do it.

00:02:35.851 --> 00:02:37.400
- (laughs) Okay.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.700
Our next stop, Bu Qtair,
where one has to try the

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.120
specialty fried fish.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.446
- They're famous for their fried fish.

00:02:45.446 --> 00:02:46.279
- OK.

00:02:46.279 --> 00:02:47.112
- And so, prawns?

00:02:47.112 --> 00:02:48.560
- Yeah, I'm really excited.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.850
Oh wow, look at that!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.230
- Here we have the Sheri
Fish, they marinated it

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.520
with masala curry.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.740
- And it's packed here, it's lunch time.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.420
- It's always packed, even
dinner, there's a queue.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.440
- [Ching] So how do we start?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.320
- You use your hands.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.799
- OK, really get the mix of spices.

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:02.632
- Yes, a nice balance.

00:03:02.632 --> 00:03:04.140
- It's got the sweetness
of the flesh of the fish.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.930
So simple, and I love
it, simplicity is key.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.220
But I want to try your food.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.940
- Yeah, why not, let's go, let's
go to my restaurant and you

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.941
see my take on doing my fish, all right?

00:03:14.941 --> 00:03:17.524
(upbeat music)

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.615
- Here we have Sea Bass Ceviche Tartare.

00:03:22.615 --> 00:03:23.879
- Uh-huh, lovely.

00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:26.147
- [Reif] And we have a (mumbles)

00:03:26.147 --> 00:03:28.520
- All in one go, that was really good,

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.230
the fish is delicious!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.780
- Yeah, we get freshly three times a week

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.350
from Japan (mumbles).

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.560
So here we have the Jet
and Bruce Lee Wagyu beef,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.980
and the rice is from Kyoto.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:40.813
- [Ching] Okay.

00:03:40.813 --> 00:03:42.583
- Only the emperor is eating this rice.

00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:46.460
- That is delicious, that
is comfort in a bowl,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.812
unbelievably delicious!

00:03:47.812 --> 00:03:49.560
- Thank you, thank you. (laughs)

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.230
Dubai is growing now,
with a lot of restaurants

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.270
opening, a lot of big chefs
coming in, it's all about

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.820
to achieve and to give
the best experience to our

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.750
customers, to our diners, you know.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.570
We do have some home-grown
restaurants, made by

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:03.963
home-grown talents as well.

00:04:05.508 --> 00:04:07.960
(upbeat music)

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.250
- [Ching] I didn't realize
that you could have such a vast

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.920
array of choice and
delicious food in Dubai.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.493
From street food to fine dining
and everything in between.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.619
My time in Dubai has been
multi-faceted, vibrant,

00:04:25.619 --> 00:04:29.440
full of flavor, full of
culture, and I can't wait

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.273
to come back.

